      "text": "# Independent incremental review: strict-whitespace successor\n\nBase 6685300af7ebdc6be93ae1e1282ffe48293f25db; frozen `admission/v2/successor83-v2.patch` SHA-256 `3103590daedf71db7c599fce5a5d0e6f4fdd78b04434cbae305209a5f4e4bd91`. No concrete blocker found for the bounded source-evidence transition. This review extends, rather than replaces, `review.md` SHA-256 `379541d9e240bfa572b52d0237deed43ac6e69738d888288354b355aebed49b0` and inherits all its runtime and coverage limits.\n\nIndependently created a fresh archive of 668 and actually applied the frozen patch using `git apply --whitespace=error`, exit 0. All 12 added/changed paths matched the frozen v2 worktree byte-for-byte. Both base64 wrappers decoded with strict validation to byte-exact Git diffs: menu SHA-256 `7a529be7861bb1a7c107d38b5aaf2ee60ecc1b2ff9a6401f435762ef51c44d4e`; field SHA-256 `af847849bc6703c84a8a8a67755f247b053510b1b6d18ca938c3b7c2fec76fc0`. The v1 review JSON, context, and prior independent report are retained byte-for-byte. For each of 83 review rows, all other v1 fields and previous evidence order are preserved; three current references replace the context and two raw patches, with three prior-history references appended. Independently rehashed 2,326 current evidence occurrences. The v1-to-v2 ledger difference is restricted to the 83 source-review bindings; no other per-row field changes. Independent executable assertions and output are in `check-v2.py` and `check-v2.json`.\n\nIndependently reran the unchanged authored-use helper and the supplied negative-control harness: 240 to 157 insufficient, exactly the 83 intended rows removed, no new rows, and the 1,736-row order retained. Wrong line, context, diff, and review reject 83; wrong relevant menu/autocomplete source or dependency rejects 41/42 respectively. Rehashed false review text remains accepted: this checker is an identity checker, not semantic validation. Its output `direct-independent-v2.json` is byte-identical to the author's retained direct result (SHA-256 `41d83314e1125ad96bde0c0367b88c21d6dc625fb78d134688c9bedf58a3436c`). The authored-use checker hashes the wrapper files but does not decode or validate their payloads; byte round-trip verification is a separate check and must not be attributed to the checker itself.\n\nNo product code, browser, fresh packed autocomplete/form-field interaction, SSR/hydration, complete matrix, security, G11 or release qualification follows from this evidence-only patch. Existing distinct menu and form-field packed evidence and historical de6 autocomplete observations retain their original subjects and limits.\n"
