      "text": "# Independent review of form-field 668 authored-use successor\n\nSubject: manifest SHA-256 `b793a5511cf16d468c922415cbbc4d495053232d681a7df4401816c4d13835e1`, source commit `6685300af7ebdc6be93ae1e1282ffe48293f25db`; per-use review SHA-256 `1187ad031ab82eed611d6230a199efdf924d852551ffb009d08a344209f49dae`, and by-triple proposal SHA-256 `f62d8eee26f98dcaf9824e0e899d94d1a98c690a0cd323981ad7103c603ef62e`. Review is limited to the exact main-line source and its existing 33 frozen triples.\n\nIndependently compared candidate disposition data to actual 668 source: all 1,736 roster identities and order match, exactly the proposed 33 form-field triples change, by-triple contains exactly those final rows, unrelated rows and non-roster metadata are identical, and all 33 complete previous ledger rows, previous review records and prior review references match the base. All referenced prior/current evidence hashes, the manifest file hashes, current integration receipt and scoped product/test images matched their retained bytes. Do not apply the entire candidate ledger over subsequent unrelated changes; compose only by exact triple against checked current prior rows.\n\nThe 33 individual conclusions remain 25 stable public peer uses, four locally owned replacements (BooleanInput and three legacy error factories), and four removed current Material token uses (ERROR, FORM_FIELD, PREFIX, SUFFIX). Reviewed current imports, constructor, query, control handling, animation policy and lifecycle source; the local aliases and factories retain distinct owned identities. The per-use decisions preserve their complete previous review and appropriately explain material changes for view timing, platform guard, native animation, cancellation, and direct hint/error wrappers. Earlier source evidence and additional current source/context images are preserved; no 21.x, security or release conclusion follows.\n\nSeparately checked newly introduced `AfterViewChecked` against installed Angular core 22.1.7 declaration: it is the public, nondeprecated interface for a callback after the view check. The current hook uses the rendered direct wrapper with a browser guard and owned lifecycle cancellation. It is correctly excluded from the old 33-row roster and has its own current-use record; its current-use owner must handle that record independently.\n\nReexecuted the unchanged direct helper in an independent output directory: insufficient 240\u2192207, exactly the 33 intended triples removed and no additions. Mutating current TS, the new review, new context, integration receipt or HTML each reopened 33; a test-only conclusion reopened one. A deliberately false decision with rehashed references remained accepted. The helper demonstrates source/evidence identity and structural sufficiency, not independent semantic truth or authorship.\n\nThe source/motion context accurately scopes prior isolated artifact `539c472f5207e7d4f5be84dd18547c22265ac6845dfef55914429844e3b2c714`: the observed form-field TS and HTML match its source map; focused Chromium zoneful/zoneless, provider/Noop/reduced, cancellation, fallback and candidate SSR evidence are bounded. Tagged 16 BrowserAnimations and Noop reference traces support Material-owned wrapper and resting style behavior. Angular-generated trigger, star and ng-tns classes are absent by the owner's engine-free decision; arbitrary consumer selector compatibility, tagged SSR, hydration, other browsers, clean current combined artifact, 21.x and full release gates remain open.\n\nConclusion: the 33 bounded source-review successor is supported subject to exact-triple integration and the independent current-use hook record; this does not grant a runtime, security, G11 or release pass.\n"
